{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"For Irish-authorised UCITS ETFs, the transparency-policy disclosure is **not** the same as publishing the full portfolio every day. The policy describes how portfolio information is made available to authorised participants (APs) and market makers to support arbitrage; disclose it in the prospectus and on the ETF’s website, as required by the 2026 regulations.\n\nThe default route is **daily public disclosure** of portfolio holdings, generally on the ETF website, with the information required by the regulations.\n\nA distinct **conditional route** permits periodic public holdings disclosure instead, but only where the ETF provides APs and market makers with daily portfolio information sufficient to facilitate arbitrage, in line with the regulatory conditions and procedures. This is not a blanket exemption from transparency: the arrangements and frequency must meet those requirements.\n\nCBI Q&A 1012 (April 2025) is relevant to the periodic-holdings route and its conditions; it should not be read as replacing the 2026 regulations or making periodic disclosure universally available."}}
